      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MISDIRECTION (1) had been in great form but missed the frame latest when sixth (23.09) in a Grade 4/5 at Gosford. Generally fast to begin but always back from the wide draw last time. Has a good record here at this journey. Won at his only start from this box. Worth another chance. ROCKIN' MIA (2) ran well two back scoring a Grade 5 win in 17.55 then out of the placings at Maitland latest but returns to a course where she has performed well. Well placed here and should do much better. JUNGLE MASTER (5) produced a moderate effort last time when seventh at Gosford over 388m behind Borrowed Times (23.28) in a Grade 5. Has ability and is one of the better chances. SUPER SKUNK (6) is worth a look over a shorter trip this time.",
